IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-periods`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), ss 202, 202A and 202B (Part 6, Division 1): the Registrar's relief from the form and content of the financial statements,
-- the directors' voluntary revision of defective statements, and the Registrar's notice and application to Court.
-- The Registrar and the Court act on the directors; the questions here are the directors' (what they may apply for, what they may do, what they must answer, what can be ordered against them).
-- What the Registrar thinks fit, is of the opinion, is satisfied with, or agrees to is a judgment the text hands to the Registrar: it is an input, never guessed.
-- Whether a company need not hold an annual general meeting under s 175A is a later wave's: an input named for the fact.
-- Section 202A(5) (the Minister's regulations under s 411) is machinery: it is a coverage row and has no function (NOTES.md, inert reason 2).

DECLARE `s 202B act` IS ONE OF
    `s 202B(2) give the Registrar the explanation, or the proposed revision, that the subsection requires`

DECLARE `s 202B(7) matter of directions` IS ONE OF
    `s 202B(7)(a) the auditing of the financial statements, or consolidated financial statements or balance sheet`
    `s 202B(7)(b) the making of revisions within a specified period`
    `s 202B(7)(c) the review by the auditors of the revised summary financial statement`
    `s 202B(7)(d) the making of necessary consequential revisions to any other document`
    `s 202B(7)(e) the taking of steps to bring the order to the notice of persons likely to rely on the previous statements`
    `s 202B(7)(f) such other matters as the Court thinks fit`

§ `Section 202(1): relief from the form and content of the statements`

-- src:18530 | 202.—(1) The directors of a company may apply to the Registrar in
-- src:18531 | writing for an order relieving them from any requirement of this Act
-- src:18532 | relating to the form and content of financial statements or
-- src:18533 | consolidated financial statements (other than a requirement of the
-- src:18534 | Accounting Standards) or to the form and content of the statement
-- src:18535 | required by section 201(16) and the Registrar may make such an
-- src:18536 | order either unconditionally or on condition that the directors comply
-- src:18537 | with such other requirements relating to the form and content of the
-- src:18538 | financial statements or consolidated financial statements or directors’
-- src:18539 | statement as the Registrar thinks fit to impose.
@ref s 202(1) (src:18530-18539)
GIVEN `the requirement relates to the form and content of the financial statements or consolidated financial statements` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirement is a requirement of the Accounting Standards` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirement relates to the form and content of the statement required by section 201(16)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 202(1) the directors may apply to the Registrar in writing for an order relieving them from the requirement` MEANS
    IF    (`the requirement relates to the form and content of the financial statements or consolidated financial statements` AND (NOT `the requirement is a requirement of the Accounting Standards`))
       OR `the requirement relates to the form and content of the statement required by section 201(16)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the grant is of "any requirement of this Act relating to the form and content of financial statements ... (other than a requirement of the Accounting Standards) or to the form and content of the statement required by section 201(16)", and a requirement outside those words is outside the grant (the grant ruling of 2026-11-12 and the "In short" line on a grant limited in its own wording; the "(other than X)" question is one of the six left to the encoder: the other reading is JUST FALSE, since the parenthesis says no to a requirement of the Accounting Standards in the text's own words)

@ref s 202(1) (src:18535-18539)
GIVEN `the other requirement relates to the form and content of the financial statements or consolidated financial statements or the directors' statement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Registrar thinks it fit to impose the other requirement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 202(1) the Registrar may make the order on condition that the directors comply with the other requirement` MEANS
    IF    `the other requirement relates to the form and content of the financial statements or consolidated financial statements or the directors' statement`
       AND `the Registrar thinks it fit to impose the other requirement`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the grant is of "such other requirements relating to the form and content of the financial statements or consolidated financial statements or directors' statement as the Registrar thinks fit to impose", and a requirement outside those words is outside the grant (the grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 1: a function named for a power whose gate failed)

§ `Section 202(4): how long the order lasts`

-- src:18571 | (4) The Registrar may make an order under subsection (1) which
-- src:18572 | may be limited to a specific period and may from time to time either
-- src:18573 | on application by the directors or without any such application (in
-- src:18574 | which case the Registrar must give to the directors an opportunity of
-- src:18575 | being heard) revoke or suspend the operation of any such order.
@ref s 202(4) (src:18571-18575)
GIVEN `the order is limited to a specific period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that specific period has ended` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Registrar has revoked the order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Registrar has suspended the operation of the order and the suspension has not ended` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 202(4) the order made under section 202(1) has not ended` MEANS
    IF    (`the order is limited to a specific period` AND `that specific period has ended`)
       OR `the Registrar has revoked the order`
       OR `the Registrar has suspended the operation of the order and the suspension has not ended`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "an order under subsection (1) which may be limited to a specific period and may from time to time either on application by the directors or without any such application ... revoke or suspend the operation of any such order" (a period the text fixes in its own words: the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (a); a revoked or suspended order has no operation to rely on)
    ELSE JUST TRUE

§ `Section 202(1) and (2): are the directors relieved?`

-- src:18530 | 202.—(1) The directors of a company may apply to the Registrar in
-- src:18531 | writing for an order relieving them from any requirement of this Act
-- src:18532 | relating to the form and content of financial statements or
-- src:18533 | consolidated financial statements (other than a requirement of the
-- src:18534 | Accounting Standards) or to the form and content of the statement
-- src:18535 | required by section 201(16) and the Registrar may make such an
-- src:18536 | order either unconditionally or on condition that the directors comply
-- src:18537 | with such other requirements relating to the form and content of the
-- src:18538 | financial statements or consolidated financial statements or directors’
-- src:18539 | statement as the Registrar thinks fit to impose.
@ref s 202(1) (src:18530-18539)
GIVEN `the Registrar has made an order on the directors' application that covers the requirement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the order is limited to a specific period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that specific period has ended` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Registrar has revoked the order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Registrar has suspended the operation of the order and the suspension has not ended` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the order was made on condition that the directors comply with other requirements` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the directors comply with those other requirements` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 202(1) the directors are relieved by the Registrar's order from the requirement` MEANS
    IF NOT `the Registrar has made an order on the directors' application that covers the requirement`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether an order exists, and what it covers, is a fact about the Registrar's own order that the text does not state
    ELSE IF `s 202(4) the order made under section 202(1) has not ended` `the order is limited to a specific period` `that specific period has ended` `the Registrar has revoked the order` `the Registrar has suspended the operation of the order and the suspension has not ended` EQUALS JUST FALSE
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "an order under subsection (1) which may be limited to a specific period and may ... revoke or suspend the operation of any such order" (see s 202(4))
         ELSE IF `the order was made on condition that the directors comply with other requirements` AND (NOT `the directors comply with those other requirements`)
              THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "make such an order either unconditionally or on condition that the directors comply with such other requirements" (an order made on condition does not relieve a director who does not meet the condition: a condition the text introduces with "on condition that")
              ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:18543 | (2) The Registrar may, where the Registrar considers it appropriate,
-- src:18544 | make an order in respect of a specified class of companies relieving
-- src:18545 | the directors of a company in that class from compliance with any
-- src:18546 | specified requirements of this Act relating to the form and content of
-- src:18547 | financial statements or consolidated financial statements (other than a
-- src:18548 | requirement of the Accounting Standards) or to the form and content
-- src:18549 | of the statement required by section 201(16) and the order may be
-- src:18550 | made either unconditionally or on condition that the directors of the
-- src:18551 | company comply with such other requirements relating to the form
-- src:18552 | and content of financial statements or consolidated financial
-- src:18553 | statements or directors’ statement as the Registrar thinks fit to
-- src:18554 | impose.
@ref s 202(2) (src:18543-18554)
GIVEN `the Registrar has made an order for a specified class of companies that includes the company and specifies the requirement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the order was made on condition that the directors comply with other requirements` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the directors comply with those other requirements` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 202(2) the directors are relieved by the Registrar's order for a class of companies from the requirement` MEANS
    IF NOT `the Registrar has made an order for a specified class of companies that includes the company and specifies the requirement`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether an order exists, which class it names and which requirements it specifies are facts about the Registrar's own order that the text does not state
    ELSE IF `the order was made on condition that the directors comply with other requirements` AND (NOT `the directors comply with those other requirements`)
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the order may be made either unconditionally or on condition that the directors of the company comply with such other requirements" (a condition the text introduces with "on condition that")
         ELSE JUST TRUE

§ `Section 202(3): the Registrar's opinion`

-- src:18561 | (3) The Registrar must not make an order under subsection (1)
-- src:18562 | unless he or she is of the opinion that compliance with the
-- src:18563 | requirements of this Act would render the financial statements or
-- src:18564 | consolidated financial statements or directors’ statement (as the case
-- src:18565 | may be) misleading or inappropriate to the circumstances of the
-- src:18566 | company or would impose unreasonable burdens on the company or
-- src:18567 | any officer of the company.
@ref s 202(3) (src:18561-18567)
GIVEN `the Registrar is of the opinion that compliance with the requirements of this Act would render the financial statements, consolidated financial statements or directors' statement misleading or inappropriate to the circumstances of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Registrar is of the opinion that compliance would impose unreasonable burdens on the company or any officer of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 202(3) the Registrar is not barred from making an order under section 202(1)` MEANS
    IF    `the Registrar is of the opinion that compliance with the requirements of this Act would render the financial statements, consolidated financial statements or directors' statement misleading or inappropriate to the circumstances of the company`
       OR `the Registrar is of the opinion that compliance would impose unreasonable burdens on the company or any officer of the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Registrar must not make an order under subsection (1) unless he or she is of the opinion that ..." (a bar closed by "unless": the grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 2)

§ `Section 202A(1): when the voluntary revision is open`

-- src:18580 | 202A.—(1) Subject to subsection (3), this section applies at any
-- src:18581 | time —
-- src:18583 | (a) in the case where a company need not hold an annual
-- src:18584 | general meeting for a financial year under section 175A —
-- src:18585 | after the financial statements or, in the case of a parent
-- src:18586 | company, consolidated financial statements and balance
-- src:18587 | sheet are sent to the members of the company under
-- src:18588 | section 203; or
-- src:18592 | (b) in any other case — after the financial statements or, in the
-- src:18593 | case of a parent company, consolidated financial
-- src:18594 | statements and balance sheet are laid before the
-- src:18595 | company at an annual general meeting.
@ref s 202A(1) (src:18580-18595)
GIVEN `the company need not hold an annual general meeting for the financial year under section 175A` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the financial statements, or consolidated financial statements and balance sheet, have been sent to the members of the company under section 203` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the financial statements, or consolidated financial statements and balance sheet, have been laid before the company at an annual general meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 202A(1) the section applies` MEANS
    IF `the company need not hold an annual general meeting for the financial year under section 175A`
    THEN (IF `the financial statements, or consolidated financial statements and balance sheet, have been sent to the members of the company under section 203`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "this section applies at any time — (a) in the case where a company need not hold an annual general meeting for a financial year under section 175A — after the financial statements ... are sent to the members of the company under section 203" (a period the text fixes in its own words: the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (a))
    ELSE (IF `the financial statements, or consolidated financial statements and balance sheet, have been laid before the company at an annual general meeting`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) in any other case — after the financial statements ... are laid before the company at an annual general meeting" (a period the text fixes in its own words: the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (a))

§ `Section 202A(2): the directors may cause the statements to be revised`

-- src:18599 | (2) Where this section applies, if it appears to the directors of the
-- src:18600 | company that the financial statements or, in the case of a parent
-- src:18601 | company, consolidated financial statements or balance sheet do not
-- src:18602 | comply with the requirements of this Act (including compliance with
-- src:18603 | the Accounting Standards), the directors may cause the financial
-- src:18604 | statements, or consolidated financial statements or balance sheet (as
-- src:18609 | the case may be), to be revised and make necessary consequential
-- src:18610 | revisions to the summary financial statement or directors’ statement.
@ref s 202A(2) (src:18599-18610)
GIVEN `the company need not hold an annual general meeting for the financial year under section 175A` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the financial statements, or consolidated financial statements and balance sheet, have been sent to the members of the company under section 203` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the financial statements, or consolidated financial statements and balance sheet, have been laid before the company at an annual general meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it appears to the directors that the financial statements, or consolidated financial statements or balance sheet, do not comply with the requirements of this Act (including the Accounting Standards)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 202A(2) the directors may cause the financial statements to be revised` MEANS
    IF `s 202A(1) the section applies` `the company need not hold an annual general meeting for the financial year under section 175A` `the financial statements, or consolidated financial statements and balance sheet, have been sent to the members of the company under section 203` `the financial statements, or consolidated financial statements and balance sheet, have been laid before the company at an annual general meeting` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN (IF `it appears to the directors that the financial statements, or consolidated financial statements or balance sheet, do not comply with the requirements of this Act (including the Accounting Standards)`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the grant is made "if it appears to the directors" that the statements do not comply, and a case outside that is outside the grant (the grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 1: a function named for a power whose `if` gate failed)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (a company's or person's liberty, no bar to relieve; S1b ruling 2026S1bC): "Where this section applies, ... the directors may cause the financial statements ... to be revised" -- a "where" gate on the directors' own liberty to revise that fails; split site (ii), fork F-202A-2 in NOTES.md (the other reading is JUST FALSE, periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b))

§ `Section 202A(3): what the revision may touch`

-- src:18614 | (3) The revision of the financial statements, or consolidated
-- src:18615 | financial statements or balance sheet (as the case may be), under
-- src:18616 | subsection (2) must be confined to —
-- src:18618 | (a) those aspects in which the financial statements, or
-- src:18619 | consolidated financial statements or balance sheet (as the
-- src:18620 | case may be), did not comply with this Act (including
-- src:18621 | compliance with the Accounting Standards); and
-- src:18623 | (b) the making of any necessary consequential revisions.
@ref s 202A(3) (src:18614-18623)
GIVEN `the revision changes something other than the aspects in which the statements did not comply with this Act and the necessary consequential revisions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 202A(3) the revision is confined as the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF `the revision changes something other than the aspects in which the statements did not comply with this Act and the necessary consequential revisions`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The revision ... must be confined to — (a) those aspects in which the financial statements ... did not comply with this Act ...; and (b) the making of any necessary consequential revisions" (a duty not met: the provision's own question, the grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 2)
    ELSE JUST TRUE

§ `Section 202A(4): after the Registrar's notice`

-- src:18627 | (4) Where the Registrar has given the directors of the company a
-- src:18628 | notice under section 202B(1), the directors may not cause the
-- src:18629 | financial statements, or consolidated financial statements or balance
-- src:18630 | sheet (as the case may be), to be revised unless the Registrar agrees
-- src:18631 | with the directors on the manner in which to revise the financial
-- src:18632 | statements, or consolidated financial statements or balance sheet (as
-- src:18633 | the case may be), referred to in section 202B(2)(b).
@ref s 202A(4) (src:18627-18633)
GIVEN `the Registrar has given the directors of the company a notice under section 202B(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Registrar agrees with the directors on the manner in which to revise the statements referred to in section 202B(2)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 202A(4) the directors are barred from causing the financial statements to be revised` MEANS
    IF NOT `the Registrar has given the directors of the company a notice under section 202B(1)`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the Registrar has given the directors of the company a notice under section 202B(1), the directors may not cause the financial statements ... to be revised unless the Registrar agrees" (a bar gated by "where": the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b): no notice, no bar from this subsection)
    ELSE IF `the Registrar agrees with the directors on the manner in which to revise the statements referred to in section 202B(2)(b)`
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may not cause the financial statements ... to be revised unless the Registrar agrees with the directors on the manner" (an "unless" once met: one of the six left to the encoder; the other reading is NOTHING)
         ELSE JUST TRUE

§ `Section 202B(1): the Registrar's notice`

-- src:18676 | 202B.—(1) If it appears to the Registrar that there is, or may be, a
-- src:18677 | question whether the financial statements or, in the case of a parent
-- src:18678 | company, consolidated financial statements and balance sheet
-- src:18679 | comply with the requirements of this Act (including compliance
-- src:18680 | with the Accounting Standards), the Registrar may give notice to the
-- src:18681 | directors of the company indicating the respects in which it appears
-- src:18682 | that such a question arises or may arise, and specify the period within
-- src:18683 | which the directors must respond.
@ref s 202B(1) (src:18676-18683)
GIVEN `it appears to the Registrar that there is, or may be, a question whether the financial statements, or consolidated financial statements and balance sheet, comply with the requirements of this Act (including the Accounting Standards)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 202B(1) the Registrar may give the directors a notice` MEANS
    IF `it appears to the Registrar that there is, or may be, a question whether the financial statements, or consolidated financial statements and balance sheet, comply with the requirements of this Act (including the Accounting Standards)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the grant is made "if it appears to the Registrar that there is, or may be, a question", and a case outside that is outside the grant (the grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 1: a function named for a power whose `if` gate failed)

§ `Section 202B(2): the directors' response`

-- The Registrar "specif[ies] the period within which the directors must respond"; the text gives no unit, so the number of days is the input (fork F-202B-days, NOTES.md).
-- "or such longer period as the Registrar may allow": the longer period is taken to be a total number of days counted from the same day as the first (fork F-202B-longer, NOTES.md).
@ref s 202B(1) (src:18680-18683)
GIVEN `the number of days the Registrar specified for the response` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of days of any longer period the Registrar has allowed` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 202B(2) the number of days allowed for the response` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the number of days of any longer period the Registrar has allowed`
    WHEN JUST longer THEN (IF longer GREATER THAN `the number of days the Registrar specified for the response` THEN longer ELSE `the number of days the Registrar specified for the response`)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `the number of days the Registrar specified for the response`

@ref s 202B(1) (src:18680-18683)
GIVEN `the day the Registrar gave the notice` IS A DATE
      `the number of days the Registrar specified for the response` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of days of any longer period the Registrar has allowed` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`s 202B(2) the last day for the directors to respond` MEANS
    `period: the last day of a period after` `the day the Registrar gave the notice` (`s 202B(2) the number of days allowed for the response` `the number of days the Registrar specified for the response` `the number of days of any longer period the Registrar has allowed`) Days

-- src:18687 | (2) The directors of the company to whom notice under
-- src:18688 | subsection (1) is given must at the end of the period mentioned in
-- src:18689 | subsection (1), or such longer period as the Registrar may allow —
-- src:18691 | (a) give the Registrar an explanation of the financial
-- src:18692 | statements, or consolidated financial statements and
-- src:18693 | balance sheet (as the case may be), if the directors do
-- src:18694 | not propose to revise the financial statements, or
-- src:18695 | consolidated financial statements or balance sheet, as the
-- src:18696 | case may be; or
-- src:18698 | (b) inform the Registrar how the directors propose to revise the
-- src:18699 | financial statements, or consolidated financial statements
-- src:18700 | or balance sheet (as the case may be), to address the
-- src:18701 | questions in respect of which the Registrar has given
-- src:18702 | notice.
@ref s 202B(2) (src:18687-18702)
GIVEN `the Registrar has given the directors notice under section 202B(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the directors propose to revise the financial statements` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 202B(2)(a) the directors must give the Registrar an explanation of the financial statements` MEANS
    IF NOT `the Registrar has given the directors notice under section 202B(1)`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is that of "the directors of the company to whom notice under subsection (1) is given", and the subsection is silent on any other directors (a scope limit with no "only": the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (c))
    ELSE IF NOT `the directors propose to revise the financial statements`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(a) give the Registrar an explanation ..., if the directors do not propose to revise the financial statements" (a duty whose "if" is unmet: one of the six left to the encoder, P-duty)

@ref s 202B(2) (src:18687-18702)
GIVEN `the Registrar has given the directors notice under section 202B(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the directors propose to revise the financial statements` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 202B(2)(b) the directors must inform the Registrar how they propose to revise the financial statements` MEANS
    IF NOT `the Registrar has given the directors notice under section 202B(1)`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is that of "the directors of the company to whom notice under subsection (1) is given", and the subsection is silent on any other directors (a scope limit with no "only": the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (c))
    ELSE IF `the directors propose to revise the financial statements`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): paragraph (b) states no condition of its own and paragraph (a) covers directors who do not propose to revise; whether (b) binds directors who do not propose to revise is not said (fork F-202B-b, NOTES.md)

@ref s 202B(2) (src:18687-18689)
GIVEN `the day the Registrar gave the notice` IS A DATE
      `the number of days the Registrar specified for the response` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of days of any longer period the Registrar has allowed` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the day the directors respond` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 202B(2) the directors responded by the end of the period` MEANS
    `the day the directors respond` AT MOST `s 202B(2) the last day for the directors to respond` `the day the Registrar gave the notice` `the number of days the Registrar specified for the response` `the number of days of any longer period the Registrar has allowed`

-- The clock counts days from the notice; the deadline is the number of days allowed (`s 202B(2) the number of days allowed for the response`).
@ref s 202B(2) (src:18687-18702)
GIVEN `the name of the director` IS A STRING
      `the number of days allowed for the response` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 202B act`
`s 202B(2) the directors must respond to the Registrar's notice by the end of the period` MEANS
    PARTY Director `the name of the director`
    MUST `s 202B(2) give the Registrar the explanation, or the proposed revision, that the subsection requires`
    WITHIN `the number of days allowed for the response`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Director `the name of the director` BECAUSE "the directors did not respond to the Registrar's notice by the end of the period allowed"

§ `Section 202B(3) and (4): after the response`

-- src:18709 | (3) If the Registrar is satisfied with the explanation of the financial
-- src:18710 | statements, or consolidated financial statements and balance sheet (as
-- src:18711 | the case may be), mentioned in subsection (2)(a), no further action
-- src:18712 | need be taken by the directors in respect of the notice under
-- src:18713 | subsection (1).
@ref s 202B(3) (src:18709-18713)
GIVEN `the directors gave the Registrar an explanation under subsection (2)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Registrar is satisfied with the explanation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 202B(3) the directors need take no further action on the notice` MEANS
    IF `the directors gave the Registrar an explanation under subsection (2)(a)` AND `the Registrar is satisfied with the explanation`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the Registrar is satisfied with the explanation ..., no further action need be taken by the directors in respect of the notice" (a condition the text introduces with "if": marginal reading (a), NOTES.md; the other reading is NOTHING, since the relief is grant-like)

-- src:18717 | (4) If the Registrar agrees with the directors on the manner in which
-- src:18718 | to revise the financial statements, or consolidated financial
-- src:18719 | statements or balance sheet (as the case may be), referred to in
-- src:18720 | subsection (2)(b), the directors may cause the financial statements, or
-- src:18721 | consolidated financial statements or balance sheet (as the case may
-- src:18722 | be), to be revised in the manner provided in section 202A.
@ref s 202B(4) (src:18717-18722)
GIVEN `the Registrar agrees with the directors on the manner in which to revise the statements referred to in subsection (2)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 202B(4) the directors may cause the financial statements to be revised in the manner agreed` MEANS
    IF `the Registrar agrees with the directors on the manner in which to revise the statements referred to in subsection (2)(b)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the grant is made "if the Registrar agrees with the directors on the manner", and a case outside that is outside the grant (the grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 1: a function named for a power whose `if` gate failed; section 202A(4) is what bars the revision)

§ `Section 202B(5) and (6): the Registrar applies to Court`

-- src:18726 | (5) The Registrar may apply to Court under subsection (6) if —
-- src:18728 | (a) the Registrar does not receive a response from the directors
-- src:18729 | after giving the notice mentioned in subsection (1);
-- src:18731 | (b) the Registrar is not satisfied with the explanation of the
-- src:18732 | financial statements, or consolidated financial statements
-- src:18733 | and balance sheet (as the case may be), mentioned in
-- src:18734 | subsection (2)(a); or
-- src:18736 | (c) the Registrar does not agree with the directors on the
-- src:18737 | manner in which the financial statements, or consolidated
-- src:18738 | financial statements or balance sheet (as the case may be),
-- src:18739 | referred to in subsection (2)(b) are to be revised.
@ref s 202B(5) (src:18726-18739)
GIVEN `the Registrar does not receive a response from the directors after giving the notice mentioned in subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Registrar is not satisfied with the explanation mentioned in subsection (2)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Registrar does not agree with the directors on the manner of revision referred to in subsection (2)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 202B(5) the Registrar may apply to Court under subsection (6)` MEANS
    IF    `the Registrar does not receive a response from the directors after giving the notice mentioned in subsection (1)`
       OR `the Registrar is not satisfied with the explanation mentioned in subsection (2)(a)`
       OR `the Registrar does not agree with the directors on the manner of revision referred to in subsection (2)(b)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the grant is made "if" one of the three cases holds, and a case outside them is outside the grant (the grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 1: a function named for a power whose `if` gate failed)

-- src:18743 | (6) An application to Court referred to in subsection (5) may be
-- src:18744 | for —
-- src:18746 | (a) a declaration that the financial statements, or consolidated
-- src:18747 | financial statements or balance sheet (as the case may be),
-- src:18748 | do not comply with the requirements of this Act (including
-- src:18749 | compliance with the Accounting Standards); and
-- src:18751 | (b) an order requiring the directors of the company to cause the
-- src:18752 | financial statements, or consolidated financial statements
-- src:18753 | or balance sheet (as the case may be), to be revised.
@ref s 202B(6) (src:18743-18753)
GIVEN `the application asks for a declaration that the financial statements do not comply with the requirements of this Act (including the Accounting Standards)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application asks for an order requiring the directors to cause the financial statements to be revised` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 202B(6) the application to Court may be for the relief` MEANS
    IF    `the application asks for a declaration that the financial statements do not comply with the requirements of this Act (including the Accounting Standards)`
       OR `the application asks for an order requiring the directors to cause the financial statements to be revised`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the application "may be for" the two reliefs listed and the subsection does not close the list with "only"

§ `Section 202B(7): the Court's directions`

-- Paragraph (f) ("such other matters as the Court thinks fit") makes the list of (a) to (e) illustrative: every matter is open to the Court once it has ordered the preparation of revised statements.
-- Paragraph (c) is gated ("where the Court has given directions under paragraph (b) to make revisions to the summary financial statement"); the catch-all in (f) leaves the answer for that matter TRUE whether or not the gate holds.
-- src:18760 | (7) Where the Court orders the preparation of revised financial
-- src:18761 | statements, or consolidated financial statements or balance sheet,
-- src:18762 | under subsection (6), it may give directions as to —
-- src:18764 | (a) the auditing of the financial statements, or consolidated
-- src:18765 | financial statements or balance sheet, as the case may be;
-- src:18767 | (b) the making of revisions to the financial statements,
-- src:18768 | consolidated financial statements, balance sheet,
-- src:18769 | directors’ statement or summary financial statement in
-- src:18770 | such manner as the Court considers necessary within a
-- src:18771 | specified period;
-- src:18773 | (c) where the Court has given directions under paragraph (b)
-- src:18774 | to make revisions to the summary financial statement, the
-- src:18775 | review by the auditors of the revised summary financial
-- src:18776 | statement;
-- src:18778 | (d) the making of necessary consequential revisions to any
-- src:18779 | other document;
-- src:18781 | (e) the taking of steps by the directors to bring the making of
-- src:18782 | the order to the notice of persons likely to rely on the
-- src:18783 | previous financial statements, consolidated financial
-- src:18784 | statements, balance sheet, directors’ statement or
-- src:18785 | summary financial statement; and
-- src:18787 | (f) such other matters as the Court thinks fit.
@ref s 202B(7) (src:18760-18787)
GIVEN `the Court has ordered the preparation of revised financial statements, or consolidated financial statements or balance sheet, under subsection (6)` IS A BOOLEAN
      matter IS A `s 202B(7) matter of directions`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 202B(7) the Court may give directions on the matter` MEANS
    IF `the Court has ordered the preparation of revised financial statements, or consolidated financial statements or balance sheet, under subsection (6)`
    THEN (CONSIDER matter
          WHEN `s 202B(7)(a) the auditing of the financial statements, or consolidated financial statements or balance sheet` THEN JUST TRUE
          WHEN `s 202B(7)(b) the making of revisions within a specified period` THEN JUST TRUE
          WHEN `s 202B(7)(c) the review by the auditors of the revised summary financial statement` THEN JUST TRUE
          WHEN `s 202B(7)(d) the making of necessary consequential revisions to any other document` THEN JUST TRUE
          WHEN `s 202B(7)(e) the taking of steps to bring the order to the notice of persons likely to rely on the previous statements` THEN JUST TRUE
          WHEN `s 202B(7)(f) such other matters as the Court thinks fit` THEN JUST TRUE)
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the Court orders the preparation of revised financial statements ..., under subsection (6), it may give directions as to —" (a "may" gated by "where": the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b); the grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 3, says do not change it and list it for the maintainer; fork F-202B-7, NOTES.md)

§ `Section 202B(8): who bears the costs`

-- src:18791 | (8) If the Court finds that the financial statements, or consolidated
-- src:18792 | financial statements or balance sheet (as the case may be), did not
-- src:18793 | comply with the requirements of this Act (including the Accounting
-- src:18794 | Standards), it may order that all or part of —
-- src:18796 | (a) the costs of or incidental to the application; and
-- src:18798 | (b) any reasonable expenses incurred by the company in
-- src:18799 | connection with or in consequence of the preparation of
-- src:18800 | revised financial statements, or consolidated financial
-- src:18801 | statements or balance sheet, as the case may be,
-- src:18803 | must be borne by any or all the directors who were directors of the
-- src:18804 | company as at the date of the directors’ statement which accompanied
-- src:18809 | the defective financial statements, or consolidated financial
-- src:18810 | statements and balance sheet, as the case may be.
@ref s 202B(8) (src:18791-18810)
GIVEN `the Court finds that the financial statements, or consolidated financial statements or balance sheet, did not comply with the requirements of this Act (including the Accounting Standards)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person was a director of the company as at the date of the directors' statement which accompanied the defective statements` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 202B(8) the Court may order that the director bears all or part of the costs and expenses` MEANS
    IF    `the Court finds that the financial statements, or consolidated financial statements or balance sheet, did not comply with the requirements of this Act (including the Accounting Standards)`
       AND `the person was a director of the company as at the date of the directors' statement which accompanied the defective statements`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the grant is made "if the Court finds" non-compliance and reaches "any or all the directors who were directors of the company as at the date of the directors' statement which accompanied the defective financial statements", and a case outside those words is outside the grant (the grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 1: a function named for a power whose `if` gate failed)

§ `Section 202B(9): revised statements revised again`

-- src:18814 | (9) The provisions of this section apply equally to revised financial
-- src:18815 | statements, or consolidated financial statements or balance sheet (as
-- src:18816 | the case may be), in which case they have effect as if the references to
-- src:18817 | revised financial statements, or consolidated financial statements or
-- src:18818 | balance sheet (as the case may be), were references to further revised
-- src:18819 | financial statements, or consolidated financial statements or balance
-- src:18820 | sheet, as the case may be.
@ref s 202B(9) (src:18814-18820)
GIVEN `the statements in question are revised financial statements, or consolidated financial statements or balance sheet` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 202B(9) the section applies to the statements as it applies to the first statements` MEANS
    IF `the statements in question are revised financial statements, or consolidated financial statements or balance sheet`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks of revised statements; the section's own application to the original statements is in subsections (1) to (8), not here
